"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T10:57:37-08:00","id":1179256,"title":"","content":"It's Changing Whey! The hardcore, ultra packed protein supplement to help you bulk up that Crinos body! Be the half ton killing monstrosity you were always meant to be with Changing Whey!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Brought to you by Magadon, Inc.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T11:29:44-08:00","id":1179268,"title":"","content":"Gut of fenris <br /> <br /> Shadow lards<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Adipose","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T17:56:46-08:00","id":1179379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1176678#post1176678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Not one peep of man hate there. I think that is important to remember, Furies were exclusively female, but they weren't man-haters. They just followed a tradition of priestesses and such to be mono-gender. Like the mythical Furies.<br /> This isn't to say this is the only way the tribe can be, but the raging man-hate came much later.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope, no peep of man hate, unless you include the worship of Artemis, who was known for eviscerating any man who tried to hit on her...<br /> <br /> Or alternatively, shooting them with arrows that magically transformed them into animals that she would then proceed to hunt down and kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T19:21:51-08:00","id":1179398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179379#post1179379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nope, no peep of man hate, unless you include the worship of Artemis, who was known for eviscerating any man who tried to hit on her...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, she made an oath to remain a virgin. It wasn't an invitation; men trying anyway strike me as being like the folks in that one comic in Subsidiaries, in the Black Dog section, where Jason O'Kelly has posted a banner reading &quot;Talk About Your Character And Die.&quot; And the fans in the comic kept doing it anyway, and died, just as promised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or alternatively, shooting them with arrows that magically transformed them into animals that she would then proceed to hunt down and kill. </div> </div> </div>Actaeon walked in on her bathing. It's not really a huge leap to assume that someone doing this has remarkably untoward aims, at which point we go back to the above. &quot;The sign's not supposed to <i>encourage</i> them...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T03:25:03-08:00","id":1179476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179379#post1179379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nope, no peep of man hate, unless you include the worship of Artemis, who was known for eviscerating any man who tried to hit on her...<br /> <br /> Or alternatively, shooting them with arrows that magically transformed them into animals that she would then proceed to hunt down and kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering her father possibly sired half of the demi-gods in the pantheon, her mother-in-law(and aunt) punished those demi-gods and whatelse, I'd say Artemis was one of the more -milder- gods. Besides, as Saur there said, Virgin goddess is not a challenge.<br /> <br /> This is why whenever I look at Scion I crack up at the poor children of Zeus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T04:35:19-08:00","id":1179484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179476#post1179476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering her father possibly sired half of the demi-gods in the pantheon, her mother-in-law(and aunt) punished those demi-gods and whatelse, I'd say Artemis was one of the more -milder- gods. Besides, as Saur there said, Virgin goddess is not a challenge.<br /> <br /> This is why whenever I look at Scion I crack up at the poor children of Zeus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Still, though. Brutally killing a man just because he thinks you're attractive is an extreme over reaction to the situation. I don't recall hearing Athena taking such measures to preserve herself. Or at least not as frequently as Artemis did.<br /> <br /> It sounds like she considered every man who ever spoke to her to be some kind of sex crazed monster who would pounce the second she let her guard down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T05:31:11-08:00","id":1179493,"title":"","content":"Ok, a bit of a tangent from the recent discussion, as I was reading Changing Ways I was, struck is too strong of a word but that's what I can come up with at the moment, by how Garou-centric it is. So I am considering writing an addendum to the book from the point of view of one of the Changing Breed, namely the Gurahl. I think it would be an interesting to work out the similarities and differences between the Breeds. For example, how do the Gurahl view the five Forms? Does regeneration work the same for all of the Changing Breeds?<br /> <br /> I don't really intend to create any mechanics for this just to get another point of view. I'd follow the same chapter layout as Changing Ways with a chapter on the nature of a Gurahl, ursine life, and magic, obviously skipping the metis chapter and possibly the pack chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T06:57:48-08:00","id":1179505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179484#post1179484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Still, though. Brutally killing a man just because he thinks you're attractive is an extreme over reaction to the situation. I don't recall hearing Athena taking such measures to preserve herself. Or at least not as frequently as Artemis did.<br /> <br /> It sounds like she considered every man who ever spoke to her to be some kind of sex crazed monster who would pounce the second she let her guard down.</div> </div> </div> </div>...to be fair, her father was Zeus. I wonder where she got THAT idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T07:39:13-08:00","id":1179511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179484#post1179484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Still, though. Brutally killing a man just because he thinks you're attractive is an extreme over reaction to the situation. I don't recall hearing Athena taking such measures to preserve herself. Or at least not as frequently as Artemis did.<br /> <br /> It sounds like she considered every man who ever spoke to her to be some kind of sex crazed monster who would pounce the second she let her guard down.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is said that the ancient greeks deliberately worked small imperfections into their artwork to avoid offending the gods. The greek pantheon is all about dramatic overreaction and regular mortals were definitionally unworthy of seeing her bathing (and presumably also of having an opinion on her appearance).<br /> <br /> Also, as the goddess of the hunt, making a mortal prey was thematic to Artemis. As the goddess of wisdom, making mortals blind was thematic to Athena. That the former seems more vicious is immaterial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 01-26-2018, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T08:13:41-08:00","id":1179518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179493#post1179493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, a bit of a tangent from the recent discussion, as I was reading Changing Ways I was, struck is too strong of a word but that's what I can come up with at the moment, by how Garou-centric it is. So I am considering writing an addendum to the book from the point of view of one of the Changing Breed, namely the Gurahl. I think it would be an interesting to work out the similarities and differences between the Breeds. For example, how do the Gurahl view the five Forms? Does regeneration work the same for all of the Changing Breeds?<br /> <br /> I don't really intend to create any mechanics for this just to get another point of view. I'd follow the same chapter layout as Changing Ways with a chapter on the nature of a Gurahl, ursine life, and magic, obviously skipping the metis chapter and possibly the pack chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it was meant to be Garou centric....its how it was always billed. Would I have liked treatment like this for each of the Changing Breeds? Sure, I'm a mokol\u00e9 fanboy, but the Garou are the central characters to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T08:29:40-08:00","id":1179521,"title":"","content":"What are the thoughts on the Gifts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T09:55:42-08:00","id":1179530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179518#post1179518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it was meant to be Garou centric....its how it was always billed. Would I have liked treatment like this for each of the Changing Breeds? Sure, I'm a mokol\u00e9 fanboy, but the Garou are the central characters to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I understood that was well. As I was reading through it I started thinking about how this could apply to other Changing Breeds, Gurahl, for me as I'm a werebear banboy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T10:31:16-08:00","id":1179538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179518#post1179518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it was meant to be Garou centric....its how it was always billed. Would I have liked treatment like this for each of the Changing Breeds? Sure, I'm a mokol\u00e9 fanboy, but the Garou are the central characters to the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can probably take the Primal-Urge systems and optional rules for regeneration with regard to Combat Healing to be universal. As for the other stuff... be careful what you wish for, because it might involve stuff worse than getting Shattered Dreams scrubbed out, or the Mokole section of Kinfolk: A Breed Apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T12:25:55-08:00","id":1179572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179538#post1179538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the other stuff... be careful what you wish for, because it might involve stuff worse than getting Shattered Dreams scrubbed out, or the Mokole section of Kinfolk: A Breed Apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I TAKE IT BACK, I TAKE IT BACK!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T14:44:40-08:00","id":1179623,"title":"","content":"To the trans-garou topic, I think it the most annoys me how being a transperson and a garou is treated as a rarity. In a species that changes shape and is tied to spirits. Mostly, because it reflects how modern people view being trans and not really how being trans is hardly an unknown thing in spiritualism. For example, if we look at why Furies keep male metis from 1st ed onwards, it is most likely in refrence to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galli\" target=\"_blank\">galli</a> (eunuchs in the service of the goddess Cybele). Given Furies in 1st ed were written as priestesses, the concept matches.<br /> <br /> Now, I already noted how the idea of being trans is hardly new in myths. But even Book of Auspices (Page 52, section Theurges and Gender) notes that garou DO in fact have a tradition of playing with gender roles, at least theurges and ragabash. A theurge who is a transwoman can draw spiritual power from her crossing that boundary that society had set for her.<br /> <br /> In less flowery terms, WtA borrows heavily from actual mystic traditions, the book only took contepolar concept of being trans into consideration.<br /> <br /> The same is actual true with how the metis section discussed homosexuality and how different tribes saw the metis breed. The constant &quot;Hey, gay sex is A-OK&quot; is refreshing but also not really very deep. Having sex with another garou even if it doesn't produce a metis has been multiple times noted as still incest. Maybe there is a push to move away from that, which I get. But I always felt with garou, it made sense. <br /> <br /> As for the tribes hating metis, I didn't mind that. But the reasonings were very shallow in some. The Wendigo only accept metis who are wendigoxwendigo, due to the lack of white blood. That says nothing but the very surface level of the tribe. Especially a tribe that would also maybe not use the term metis of the breed. Going deeper and explaining cultural reasons of metis hate would have given a more complete picture.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T01:49:11-08:00","id":1180099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179484#post1179484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Still, though. Brutally killing a man just because he thinks you're attractive is an extreme over reaction to the situation. I don't recall hearing Athena taking such measures to preserve herself. Or at least not as frequently as Artemis did.<br /> <br /> It sounds like she considered every man who ever spoke to her to be some kind of sex crazed monster who would pounce the second she let her guard down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't find a myth where she kills a guy that doesn't have some variant of &quot;and he tried to rape her&quot;. That isn't to say there aren't versions where the guy seems to be just a peeper but there seems to always be another telling that was &quot;yeah it wasn't just peeping..&quot; so maybe this is the issue? <br /> <br /> Come to think of it I can't really think of any &quot;guy chases Athena&quot; narratives though I'm sure those exist but they haven't stuck into my mind and if people aren't explicitly hunting Athena it would explain why she doesn't have stories of &quot;fuck off and die asshole&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T02:55:56-08:00","id":1180109,"title":"","content":"I am sad I din't see a rework on old Lupus and Metis gifts, like Boon of the Animal Fathers and Umbral Body. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Though I am glad about the rework on Combat Healing, I was howling for years about it.<br /> I love you White Wolf &lt;3 !!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 01-28-2018, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T07:57:39-08:00","id":1180164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179623#post1179623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The same is actual true with how the metis section discussed homosexuality and how different tribes saw the metis breed. The constant &quot;Hey, gay sex is A-OK&quot; is refreshing but also not really very deep. Having sex with another garou even if it doesn't produce a metis has been multiple times noted as still incest. Maybe there is a push to move away from that, which I get. But I always felt with garou, it made sense.<br /> <br /> As for the tribes hating metis, I didn't mind that. But the reasonings were very shallow in some. The Wendigo only accept metis who are wendigoxwendigo, due to the lack of white blood. That says nothing but the very surface level of the tribe. Especially a tribe that would also maybe not use the term metis of the breed. Going deeper and explaining cultural reasons of metis hate would have given a more complete picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>WtA has long played with the idea if homosexuality was against the litany or not. Heck Revised Black Furies, and CoG basically flat out states its ok. I want to say I read somewhere (or it was our table's cannon) however that most tribes in the past were not ok with it because it was seen as &quot;cheating&quot; the system basically. Heterosexual Garou resented the same sex relationships because they could be together and not risk breaking the litany. It was seen as the basis for any homophobia in the nation, combined with the concept of sleeping with a Garou being culturally the same as incest.<br /> <br /> Metis: I can understand wanting a deeper analysis of the tribes and their stances on why they mistreat the Metis. Granted in my opinion, I'm not sure how much each tribe really needs their own spin on &quot;why&quot; since I thought it was more a Garou thing and not a tribal culture thing. I AM glad it seems with the Fianna they are moving more to just caring about the litany and less about that whole stupid &quot;Perfect of Mind, Perfect of Body&quot; garbage that I felt never made any sense with the Garou and odd that a concept from the early Iron age survived to this modern day (esp since it was so at odds with Garou culture &quot;don't get a battle scar or you'll lose your position as alpha!&quot;)<br /> <br /> Gifts:<br /> <br /> &quot;Blood Life&quot; the lvl 2 Theurge gift where you get flashes of memory through bite attacks. Personally in my own games I'm going to also rule it as a generic Mokole gift, due to its link with history and memories (I've done stuff like this in the past, like ruling that the Fianna/Galliard gift &quot;Reverie&quot; from the revised Fianna book also was a Mokole gift).<br /> <br /> Building a Legand: Some of my friends and I got into a discussion no this one....some of us argue that it means you get will when you perform an act that would grant reknown, others of us (like myself) feel its when you officially receive the reknown. Thoughs?<br /> <br /> Go for the Jugular: I was glad to see it get a downgrade....before it was more powerful then Fenris' Bite which was level 5...I'm ok with a +3 diff to soak (still powerful and handy but not exactly beating a lvl 5 gift). I was originally worried unsoakable bite attacks at the cost of only a Rage would add into the issue of the cliche Lupus Ahroun Star Gazer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T10:15:53-08:00","id":1180195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1180164#post1180164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WtA has long played with the idea if homosexuality was against the litany or not. Heck Revised Black Furies, and CoG basically flat out states its ok. I want to say I read somewhere (or it was our table's cannon) however that most tribes in the past were not ok with it because it was seen as &quot;cheating&quot; the system basically. Heterosexual Garou resented the same sex relationships because they could be together and not risk breaking the litany. It was seen as the basis for any homophobia in the nation, combined with the concept of sleeping with a Garou being culturally the same as incest.<br /> <br /> Metis: I can understand wanting a deeper analysis of the tribes and their stances on why they mistreat the Metis. Granted in my opinion, I'm not sure how much each tribe really needs their own spin on &quot;why&quot; since I thought it was more a Garou thing and not a tribal culture thing. I AM glad it seems with the Fianna they are moving more to just caring about the litany and less about that whole stupid &quot;Perfect of Mind, Perfect of Body&quot; garbage that I felt never made any sense with the Garou and odd that a concept from the early Iron age survived to this modern day (esp since it was so at odds with Garou culture &quot;don't get a battle scar or you'll lose your position as alpha!&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it being a question has been good. To me, the book just constantly stating that it is fine feels a bit weird, given the previous ambiguity about it. I'm not -against- it, but I don't think it needed to be discussed like this. Nor the incest aspect ignored.<br /> <br /> For the metis, the whole 'Why hasn't this been a problem?' about Fianna and disabilities is why I think more in-depth explanations are needed. These tribes have diverged from one another a lot, in all the millenia the garou have been around, there should be a wide variety of takes to it. Especially with the Wendigo, where metis is a term for a group of people in their territory and how cliche their opinion was.<br /> <br /> Plus, given the whole 'breeding metis for war' thing has been treated as acceptable, maybe some times could have had a tradition of that in the past?<br /> <br /> One thing I realised that is missing in the lupus section, is discussion on wolfdogs, coywolves and such. With modern knowledge of wolves, especially in USA, it could have been very interesting to consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T10:37:10-08:00","id":1180199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1180195#post1180195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Especially with the Wendigo, where metis is a term for a group of people in their territory and how cliche their opinion was.<br /> <br /> Plus, given the whole 'breeding metis for war' thing has been treated as acceptable, maybe some times could have had a tradition of that in the past?<br /> <br /> One thing I realised that is missing in the lupus section, is discussion on wolfdogs, coywolves and such. With modern knowledge of wolves, especially in USA, it could have been very interesting to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Wendigo...do you think they'd invent a new word because the humans in their area are using a similar word (since its Metis is supposed to be Garou in game....)? Or do you think there should have been some sort of aside with the Wendigo opinion on the entire matter? <br /> <br /> For Wolf Dogs, I think the 2nd ed BotW or first Kinfolk book covered them as favorites for the Spirals....didn't they? As for the Coyote and wolf blood mixing in N. America could have been interesting to see written about. Where exactly is the line between Nuwisha and Garou.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T11:54:13-08:00","id":1180214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1180199#post1180199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the Wendigo...do you think they'd invent a new word because the humans in their area are using a similar word (since its Metis is supposed to be Garou in game....)? Or do you think there should have been some sort of aside with the Wendigo opinion on the entire matter?<br /> <br /> For Wolf Dogs, I think the 2nd ed BotW or first Kinfolk book covered them as favorites for the Spirals....didn't they? As for the Coyote and wolf blood mixing in N. America could have been interesting to see written about. Where exactly is the line between Nuwisha and Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>An aside would have been good, and a motive to dislike metis that isn't 'white people's fault'.<br /> <br /> Yeah, but those books were written a while ago. Science has progressed from those times, and the knowledge of wolves has changed a lot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T14:02:28-08:00","id":1180242,"title":"","content":"I generally assume that the instinct for competitive dominance is something human that surges with the First Change for lupus Garou, the way the animalistic instinct to hunt surges in Homid Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T15:29:28-08:00","id":1180267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1180242#post1180242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally assume that the instinct for competitive dominance is something human that surges with the First Change for lupus Garou, the way the animalistic instinct to hunt surges in Homid Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not really the kind of behavior that would awaken. Facility with language to communicate with those around the new, different body, yes. Fiddling around with the new hands that have an oddly large amount of sensation in them as if they were a weird replacement for the nose and ears of the wolf, sure. Trying to be the king of the hill, however, is more of an individual thing, and scaring others into compliance is more what I'd term playing to genre as being a monster in a horror game. After all, neither humans nor wolves have Rage, but it is a fundamental part of being this variety of werewolf, and facilitates doing werewolf kind of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T04:30:11-08:00","id":1180380,"title":"","content":"The Rites/Gifts chapter is pretty good, telling a story and discussing garou relationship with Gifts/Rites at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T04:33:28-08:00","id":1180381,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">No I think the king of the hill thing makes total sense. You change one day, probably after the slaughter of innocents that you'll have some complex around, and you're a god among men. Small caliber bullets are merely painful, you can regenerate your limbs, you've got access to four new, interesting and useful forms, you can have any &quot;sheep&quot; you want with your animal attraction, willpower depending. The rage intolerance of humans will probably have you lose respect for more and more of them as it increases and begins to overpower. Then your new culture will give you kinfolk and they will be considered </span></span><i>yours </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If that doesn't breed bad people, I don't know what will. Now, the obvious downside here is that there are other garou, and they're not automatically less than you. In fact, they're the only individuals that could potentially be greater than you. For some garou (not all), I imagine their needs to be a pecking order here, because domestically those garou are so used to power that they need clear lines to make sure they don't overstep. For others they're just happy to be with others like them, they're willing to go with the flow, or have some sensible rationalisation/like another enough to be content with groups that form. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Wolves have affairs too, I imagine the whole &quot;honourably mated&quot; tenet is to stop Garou killing eachother over many kinfolk disputes. Most of the rules, really, are to stop very powerful and prideful individuals from tearing themselves apart. Garou are horrible people who distract themselves with noble and altruistic goals to satisfy their conscience.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1179623#post1179623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the trans-garou topic, I think it the most annoys me how being a transperson and a garou is treated as a rarity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, firstly trans people are relatively rare, and Garou are even rarer, but I think the issue past that is that garou are just too goddamn horrible to accept them. Maybe one or two tribes are nominal exceptions, but garou are very &quot;tribal&quot; in mentality, with a real -be-like-us- kind of bent, they don't respond well to difference. Of course, if your world of darkness is less pessimistically-realist than mine, then make your changes. I think you're too good for garou. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>We play one goddamn spiral game and the view of gaian garou has forever changed. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":23728,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","user":"PewPew","date":". 01-29-2018, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T06:11:34-08:00","id":1180402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1180381#post1180381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, firstly trans people are relatively rare, and Garou are even rarer, but I think the issue past that is that garou are just too goddamn horrible to accept them. Maybe one or two tribes are nominal exceptions, but garou are very &quot;tribal&quot; in mentality, with a real -be-like-us- kind of bent, they don't respond well to difference. Of course, if your world of darkness is less pessimistically-realist than mine, then make your changes. I think you're too good for garou. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>We play one goddamn spiral game and the view of gaian garou has forever changed. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sure, garou nation is very tribal and very close minded at parts. But once again, it isn't the same way that human society can be. As I pointed out in my post, the concept of theurges and ragabash transcending gender is canon. Not to mention, it is very much a real mystical thing to go past your expected limits and gain power from it.<br /> <br /> Basically, Nation can be horrible but not in the same way that our culture can be. Not to mention, Luna changes her face constantly, garou change their forms and Wyld is a force of constant change. Is it so hard to see the idea of transcending gender as also something garou would be less strict about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T07:20:28-08:00","id":1180411,"title":"","content":"Yes but garou flip their shit when you change auspice or tribe, and garou don't really understand the wyld too well, often mistaking many of their spirits for wyrmish ones. I feel guilty even thinking of explaining how I think garou might see the act. I think a few of the more horrible tribes probably see gender change as a problem as bad as metis or...<br /> This is a painful post.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Many would assume gender change among garou is a problem that's a mild metis flaw, about as serious as albinism, being intersex or having horns</div></div> </div> </div><br /> It's a game, it's supposed to be fun, so ignore that, but if you treat it as literature/social comentary like I do then things can get very dark and very uncomfortable.<br /> Mage and vampire? More than accepting. Werewolf... Garou are total assholes. I don't really want to go into the views of every tribe individually, as they vary, but I believe most would be antagonistic. It's a game, you don't need it to be miserable, do whatever you want. I like challenge, but that kind of uphill climb with something that affects you in real life might not be worth it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":23728,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","user":"PewPew","date":". 01-29-2018, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T10:34:50-08:00","id":1180452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1180411#post1180411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but garou flip their shit when you change auspice or tribe, and garou don't really understand the wyld too well, often mistaking many of their spirits for wyrmish ones. I feel guilty even thinking of explaining how I think garou might see the act. I think a few of the more horrible tribes probably see gender change as a problem as bad as metis or...<br /> This is a painful post.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Many would assume gender change among garou is a problem that's a mild metis flaw, about as serious as albinism, being intersex or having horns</div></div> </div> </div><br /> It's a game, it's supposed to be fun, so ignore that, but if you treat it as literature/social comentary like I do then things can get very dark and very uncomfortable.<br /> Mage and vampire? More than accepting. Werewolf... Garou are total assholes. I don't really want to go into the views of every tribe individually, as they vary, but I believe most would be antagonistic. It's a game, you don't need it to be miserable, do whatever you want. I like challenge, but that kind of uphill climb with something that affects you in real life might not be worth it</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit I don't agree. You are seeing the trans situation from the perspective of a modern person where such hate happens towards trans people happens. But garou do not share all of those beliefs to justify such hatred towards trans people. For one, minus the Black Furies, garou really don't seem too much into gender-roles. Older books did have pretty hilarious crap with Fenrir not accepting ahroun females, but generally from the books the gender roles have been very minimal. Unlike auspice roles, the Book of Auspices notes that changing your auspice is like reconstructive surgery to us. That is the difference, I think. It is not as much the gender that matters as what Auspice ones is. Hence why the issues of changing auspice and tribe, those matter. Gender to non-Furies is not as big of a deal or given the theurge chapter, transcending it might even be looked as favourable.<br /> <br /> As for the relation to metis flaw, well, let us remember that metis deformities and regular disfigurements are generally seen differently. There are plenty of physical and mental disability flaws that aren't solely metis deformities, but they aren't stated to be seen as making the non-metis equal to a metis. Metis hate, to me, comes from the whole Litany break and cultural things outside deformities.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T12:52:41-08:00","id":1180477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1180381#post1180381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">No I think the king of the hill thing makes total sense. You change one day, probably after the slaughter of innocents that you'll have some complex around, and you're a god among men. Small caliber bullets are merely painful, you can regenerate your limbs, you've got access to four new, interesting and useful forms, you can have any &quot;sheep&quot; you want with your animal attraction, willpower depending. The rage intolerance of humans will probably have you lose respect for more and more of them as it increases and begins to overpower. Then your new culture will give you kinfolk and they will be considered </span></span><i>yours </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, it's not being driven by being human or wolf. Also, you might end up roughly disabused of your riding high in the manner that the 1e Player's Guide intro fiction narrator was if you don't band together with others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If that doesn't breed bad people, I don't know what will. Now, the obvious downside here is that there are other garou, and they're not automatically less than you. In fact, they're the only individuals that could potentially be greater than you. For some garou (not all), I imagine their needs to be a pecking order here, because domestically those garou are so used to power that they need clear lines to make sure they don't overstep. For others they're just happy to be with others like them, they're willing to go with the flow, or have some sensible rationalisation/like another enough to be content with groups that form. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Wolves have affairs too, I imagine the whole &quot;honourably mated&quot; tenet is to stop Garou killing eachother over many kinfolk disputes. Most of the rules, really, are to stop very powerful and prideful individuals from tearing themselves apart. Garou are horrible people who distract themselves with noble and altruistic goals to satisfy their conscience.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Wolves live in family units unless they're captive. Also, that standpoint of &quot;Garou are just putting on a gloss&quot; is a bit too cynical to play the game straight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Well, firstly trans people are relatively rare, and Garou are even rarer, but I think the issue past that is that garou are just too goddamn horrible to accept them. Maybe one or two tribes are nominal exceptions, but garou are very &quot;tribal&quot; in mentality, with a real -be-like-us- kind of bent, they don't respond well to difference. Of course, if your world of darkness is less pessimistically-realist than mine, then make your changes. I think you're too good for garou. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>You're not being a realist here. Just a pessimist, for a particularly intense value of one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>We play one goddamn spiral game and the view of gaian garou has forever changed. </i> </div> </div> </div>BSDs act like vampires. Vampires thrive on lying to themselves and to others. Something to keep in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T13:46:16-08:00","id":1180495,"title":"","content":"I'd say that Garou nature likes closer to ronin/skindancers prides than the nation or the spirals. The freedom of the spirals is closer than the rigid rules of the nation to werewolf nature, but the garou are meant to be balanced, and dedicating yourself to one aspect of the triat's obviously a stupid move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":23728,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","user":"PewPew","date":". 01-29-2018, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T16:08:38-08:00","id":1180527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1180402#post1180402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it so hard to see the idea of transcending gender as also something garou would be less strict about?</div> </div> </div> </div>To me? Yes.<br /> <br /> But there's certainly nothing stopping you from being less restrictive in your own games. <br /> <br /> I know that Phil Brucato writes Mage with more of a magical sense surrounding trans people than other writers do. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T16:21:48-08:00","id":1180529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1180495#post1180495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd say that Garou nature likes closer to ronin/skindancers prides than the nation or the spirals. The freedom of the spirals is closer than the rigid rules of the nation to werewolf nature, but the garou are meant to be balanced, and dedicating yourself to one aspect of the triat's obviously a stupid move.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou Nation is only a bit behind the Ahadi and the Beast Courts. And in the end, they're meant to be with Gaia and Gaian spirits, not with loners who just barely survive day to day or disgruntled kin who ritually murdered a bunch of their relatives and ended up diving headlong toward the Wyrm for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T20:30:04-08:00","id":1180591,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, an inescapable issue with the foundations of WtA, is that the game has presented the Garou as completely inconsistent in when they're an ancient culture with values very separated from modern ones, and when they've got a more modern stance on an issue.<br /> <br /> The Silver Fangs flop around between a broader sense of royalty where royals do something or get deposed quickly, or late monarchs where family is everything and generations of small groups of family lines have stayed in power with just bickering between themselves on who's on the throne. Why would the Fangs ever abandon ancient concepts of royalty for a model of late European hereditary monarchies?<br /> <br /> On one hand, it makes sense that Garou attitudes adapt over time, but the books don't present a reliable idea of how much influence human cultures have (or why some cultures impact things more than others).<br /> <br /> We also have to consider ancient beliefs in context. Greek mythology and thoughts on things like sex, gender, and gender-roles where in a very different context then modern views on the subject. Just like Iran recognizes sexual reassignment surgery as acceptable as long as you intend to live as a heterosexual once transitioned, but considers homosexuality wrong, based on a specific interpretation of Islamic theology, we can't just assume the Black Furies are going to hold views essentially in line with current LGBTQ rights advocates because ancient Greek mythology isn't in line with anti-LGBTQ ideologies. The Furies might be... well fairly in-line with Changing Ways: changing your gender is a spiritual thing, not something done with medical solutions. Doing it for secular reasons founded in humanist thinking isn't necessarily an argument the Furies would accept. <br /> <br /> I mean, it's really, really, not hard to redo WtA to fix these things... but it's hard to just retcon it without just making things more of a jumble. The game could use a decent reset instead of just more retcons with each edition (and we know those aren't always positive anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T20:36:02-08:00","id":1180593,"title":"","content":"Resets scare me...while I may lose what I hate....I may also lose what I love in the game (I've got issues)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T23:19:50-08:00","id":1180621,"title":"","content":"This is why it is best for some of these issues to be decided at individual gaming groups rather than presenting an official position. Most of these social issues have zero applicability to games. Each group should be able to come up with something that works for them - if it becomes a thing in their game - and not have to worry about whether it conflicts or supports canon. Game materials should be more about things that can support the game that the individual STs are trying to create, not trying to force them to run their game along a certain line.<br /> <br /> Give more examples of appropriate Challenges for the ranks. Give more examples of good Chiminage ideas for spirits for various tasks. Give more examples of caern types along with appropriate caern powers that can be tapped. Give examples of common spirit quests in the umbra to accomplish certain things. Go into more detail on the totem bans and show how they can add to the game. Give more write up of septs along the length of the Sept of the Green in 1st/2nd edition corebook that go into detail on sept leadership styles, magic of the bawn, and showcase the differences between tribes.<br /> <br /> Those kind of things give tools to the ST to run their games and inspire them. It'll also answer a lot of common questions STs have when running the game. That helps people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T00:27:16-08:00","id":1180636,"title":"","content":"Well, we're not getting a reset anyway. It was meant more as an observation than anything else.<br /> <br /> As for the applicability of social issues to games? Well, actually, it does help to address them if you're going to have groups that care about them in the game. Presenting groups like the Tribes in a coherent (not homogeneous, there can be internal disagreements for lots of hooks and such) fashion helps people playing the game.<br /> <br /> If you present a group with to contradictory mainstream beliefs, and don't clarify how the group deals with that in their methods, traditions, and norms, then STs don't know how to present them, and players don't know how to react to things.<br /> <br /> For example, the Black Furies have two contradictory mainstream beliefs: &quot;Males can't be members of the Tribe,&quot; and, &quot;Metis males can be members of the Tribe.&quot; We have a coherent explanation for this: Pegasus allows it as a spiritual matter, and the Furies respond to this by slotting Metis into the crones due to their infertility to fit them into their larger traditions and norms. If we didn't have that and were just told that there aren't male Furies, but there are male Metis Furies... not having even a simple explanation of why that's the case, and how it looks in practice would make the concept extremely frustrating to use in play.<br /> <br /> Just saying that the Black Furies fight the oppression of women without explaining what that means in a significant fashion so groups can decide themselves doesn't really work. The game brought the social issue of feminism into the game already. Giving zero framework for what &quot;fighting the oppression of women,&quot; means isn't helping people run the game.<br /> <br /> If you cut out this sort of thing... well you might as well be playing Forsaken. This isn't meant as a judgement. Forsaken goes the route of Tribes that don't directly incorporate human social issues, and each Pack and Protectorate has it's own politics so the players and ST can include whatever they want to address in game. Some people prefer that. Some people prefer the WoD's tying of splats to real world issues. Some people want one or the other based on their mood. <br /> <br /> But since we're talking about WtA, we're talking about a game with splats that are tied to these issues. Not exploring them at all in the text is unhelpful as not exploring some of the things you talked about. They're also not mutually exclusive either. We have books like W20 Rage Across the World to look at more example Caerns, or W20 Umbra to talk about chiminage and stuff to do on spirit quests. If you want to make the case that the books that should be addressing all that stuff didn't focus on things well? Cool, you probably have a strong point. Changing Ways failed to do lots of things well. But it certainly is a book that's a logical place to explore some of these things in more detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T11:54:05-08:00","id":1180829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1180195#post1180195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I realised that is missing in the lupus section, is discussion on wolfdogs, coywolves and such. With modern knowledge of wolves, especially in USA, it could have been very interesting to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>My current character is a lupus ragabash, born a red wolf in North Carolina. A rude Uktena said he was Nuwisha, and the only thing that convinced the Uktena otherwise is that my character's mother is a Theurge. But there's probably coyote blood somewhere in his ancestry, which is what raised the Uktena's eyebrow in the first place. So yeah, that would be an interesting question to explore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T12:08:37-08:00","id":1181460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1169308#post1169308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wendigo focus on metis is really stereotypical. There were no metis among them until the whites came, because they killed them at birth. Given the chapter out and out states that metis are abused disabled children, here I would have liked more research on how the native american nations Wendigo consider their own actually handled disabled children.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this was way back, but I can answer this. Among a lot of Native peoples the Wendigo would have taken kin with, disabled people were considered blessed. It was seen as the Creator had taken something from them so they could be gifted with more spiritual power. Intersex people, little people, etc were often medicine people. So this makes no fucking sense except, IMO, as trying to turn the Wendigo into more of an 'asshole tribe' to balance out the noble savagery that was prevalent in earlier editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T12:55:33-08:00","id":1181473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1181460#post1181460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know this was way back, but I can answer this. Among a lot of Native peoples the Wendigo would have taken kin with, disabled people were considered blessed. It was seen as the Creator had taken something from them so they could be gifted with more spiritual power. Intersex people, little people, etc were often medicine people. So this makes no fucking sense except, IMO, as trying to turn the Wendigo into more of an 'asshole tribe' to balance out the noble savagery that was prevalent in earlier editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much for the information ^^<br /> <br /> This is why I think doing research on how cultures that have garou tribes tied to them, is so important. The surface level 'no metis until whites came' does not tell you anything new and at the same time doesn't tell of what sort of culture Wendigo would have with disabled members of their tribe. I don't mean that garou culture and the human cultures should be entirely similar, but rooting out things like how they deal with disability and then using it to inform what the tribes should think of their metis members, would give a more nuanced and varied collection of opinions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:26:00-08:00","id":1181650,"title":"","content":"Just because the humans do something doesn't mean the garou do. Greece has always been patriarchal, and look at the tribe they spawned. The Get have a completely reversed take of Norse mythology with fenrir being a top bloke with Odin et al being diabolical. If the wendigo practice beliefs very different from their human populace, that isn't so significant, though it'd be nice if they singled it out and mentioned it for the uninformed. Not to mention the wendigo make up a tiny, tiny, tiny percentage of native americans, who are themselves less than 5% of the canadian population and are significantly less in the US.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar21481_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"21481\" data-vbnamecard=\"21481\">Onkwe</a> could you cite sources? It's a topic with a lot of bias and I'd like something concrete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T08:30:37-08:00","id":1181666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1181650#post1181650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because the humans do something doesn't mean the garou do. Greece has always been patriarchal, and look at the tribe they spawned. The Get have a completely reversed take of Norse mythology with fenrir being a top bloke with Odin et al being diabolical. If the wendigo practice beliefs very different from their human populace, that isn't so significant, though it'd be nice if they singled it out and mentioned it for the uninformed. Not to mention the wendigo make up a tiny, tiny, tiny percentage of native americans, who are themselves less than 5% of the canadian population and are significantly less in the US.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those differences were due to the creators picking up random bits of mythology, deciding to make werewolves off of them, and then having to work around the consequences. On the other end of the spectrum, you have a lot of other tribes; Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers are the most visible of them, but the Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs are deeply embroiled in feudal practices (the Hakken Shadow Lords in particular), and the Silent Striders didn't have an inherently acrimonious relationship with Ancient Egyptian culture, having the benefit of appearing like Anpw in Crinos. We also have long-standing lore that the Croatan, Uktena, and Wendigo were closer to humanity in the Americas than the other tribes in the Old World, to the point of never getting around to the Impergium, so there's also that to consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T08:40:19-08:00","id":1181672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1181650#post1181650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because the humans do something doesn't mean the garou do. Greece has always been patriarchal, and look at the tribe they spawned. The Get have a completely reversed take of Norse mythology with fenrir being a top bloke with Odin et al being diabolical. If the wendigo practice beliefs very different from their human populace, that isn't so significant, though it'd be nice if they singled it out and mentioned it for the uninformed. Not to mention the wendigo make up a tiny, tiny, tiny percentage of native americans, who are themselves less than 5% of the canadian population and are significantly less in the US.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar21481_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"21481\" data-vbnamecard=\"21481\">Onkwe</a> could you cite sources? It's a topic with a lot of bias and I'd like something concrete.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, there is a world of difference between having Fenrir break cultural traditions (though, I rather add them back myself) than Wendigo. Because the nordic voice is much easier to find and is a much more loud one than the First Nations voice. Especially for those that live outside America, that voice is often given secondhand if at all. As sad as it is, WtA has been one of the more serious sources for First Nations knowledge for me rather than just the surface level.<br /> <br /> So the metis Wendigo part -only- saying 'Wendigo hate white people and think they are purer than others' is doing a great disservice to the First Nations people the tribe is based on. Because an alternative voice is not as easy to find as a nordic one.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Sami are here, but they aren't the American cultures Wendigo are based on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T15:43:54-08:00","id":1181828,"title":"","content":"I knew about a lot of the First Nation views of disability before, through both college and my own family. I used to go on rants about how I could see the Uktena and Wendigo being more accepting of the Metis, but it felt there were just too many tribes that were according to their tribe books. For the record not only did Wendigo kin view disabilities and variations this way, but Uktena kin too (for example many Meso-American cultures viewed Down Syndrome as a sign of the Jaguar and held those individuals as sacred).<br /> <br /> For me, they could have thought up a more Garou cultured reason (like fear of abandoning their kin, or a huge respect for the litany) that didn't lean on human racial issues, or flew directly in the face of kin culture. If I had a dime for the amount of times people I met made assumptions on human cultures based on the Garou tribes, I'd .....be able to get a pizza? You get my point though its been too many (I brought this concern up in the Shattered Dreams KS when it was mentioned that the book depicts Europeans as the first Homo sapiens to enter the Americas). To depict the Wendigo as rather Spartan in this case can cause poor assumptions about cultures that are often misunderstood (For better or worse).<br /> <br /> Personally I just wanted to see more tribes have a generally more negative view of the metis, if the metis really are meant to be this oppressed breed that faces a great deal of discrimination. In Revised it felt more like if you just avoid the Fangs, Talons, and Fianna you were going to be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 02-02-2018, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T16:51:05-08:00","id":1181849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1181828#post1181828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, they could have thought up a more Garou cultured reason (like fear of abandoning their kin, or a huge respect for the litany) that didn't lean on human racial issues, or flew directly in the face of kin culture. If I had a dime for the amount of times people I met made assumptions on human cultures based on the Garou tribes, I'd .....be able to get a pizza? You get my point though its been too many (I brought this concern up in the Shattered Dreams KS when it was mentioned that the book depicts Europeans as the first Homo sapiens to enter the Americas). To depict the Wendigo as rather Spartan in this case can cause poor assumptions about cultures that are often misunderstood (For better or worse).<br /> <br /> Personally I just wanted to see more tribes have a generally more negative view of the metis, if the metis really are meant to be this oppressed breed that faces a great deal of discrimination. In Revised it felt more like if you just avoid the Fangs, Talons, and Fianna you were going to be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, even just having the Wendigo POV mention -why- they do not follow their kins' way would have been helpful. For me, I just like adding Finnish culture stuff into Fenrir because my country is not that well known. But just <i>&quot;The metis are not blessed by the spirits, like some of our medicine people are. Their deformities are always unnatural and signs of Gaia's disfavour&quot; </i>would have said enough to justify the harsh treatment. Rather than saying basically nothing.<br /> <br /> I think this book actually did a much better job than Guardians of the Caerns, in that it focused on what education metis might have or how their treatment varied across the board even among the same tribe. Fenrir being accepting of those worthy to keeping metis as attack dogs depending on the area they are from makes sense. Guardians of the Caerns focused too much on the angst and the narrator, rather than factoids like education or alternative takes on each tribe. I do think having a negative and positive Children of Gaia would have worked, but I think the tribe being a hot mess is pretty much canon now.<br /> <br /> To me, it also had more examples of varied metis treatment outside beatings and mental abuse, discussing the fact that metis could easily be zealots due to how they are taught and the aformentioned attack dog and cannon fodder metis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T17:13:57-08:00","id":1181859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1181849#post1181849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, even just having the Wendigo POV mention -why- they do not follow their kins' way would have been helpful. For me, I just like adding Finnish culture stuff into Fenrir because my country is not that well known. But just <i>&quot;The metis are not blessed by the spirits, like some of our medicine people are. Their deformities are always unnatural and signs of Gaia's disfavour&quot; </i>would have said enough to justify the harsh treatment. Rather than saying basically nothing.<br /> <br /> I think this book actually did a much better job than Guardians of the Caerns, in that it focused on what education metis might have or how their treatment varied across the board even among the same tribe. Fenrir being accepting of those worthy to keeping metis as attack dogs depending on the area they are from makes sense. Guardians of the Caerns focused too much on the angst and the narrator, rather than factoids like education or alternative takes on each tribe. I do think having a negative and positive Children of Gaia would have worked, but I think the tribe being a hot mess is pretty much canon now.<br /> <br /> To me, it also had more examples of varied metis treatment outside beatings and mental abuse, discussing the fact that metis could easily be zealots due to how they are taught and the aformentioned attack dog and cannon fodder metis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can pretty much agree with everything in this post. I actually want to make a pack of the attack Fenrir Metis and have my players stumble on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T18:10:08-08:00","id":1182456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1181650#post1181650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar21481_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"21481\" data-vbnamecard=\"21481\">Onkwe</a> could you cite sources? It's a topic with a lot of bias and I'd like something concrete.</div> </div> </div> </div>The elders of of my tribes.<br /> <br /> Garou are Garou, but the way Changing Ways has it written is kind of stupid and lacks any sort of nuance or reflection of why the Wendigo would change their ways in regards to the Metis. There's a lot of other ways to make them have negative traits than making them into Blood Quantum warriors and projecting Euro-American 'Barbarian' stereotypes onto them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 02-04-2018, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T19:19:41-08:00","id":1182475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169198-changing-ways-thoughts?p=1182456#post1182456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The elders of of my tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea I had my own family, which was reinforced by professors for this. I haven't bothered to look for books or websites to back me up because it was stuff I grew up with as well. Its just a matter of a &quot;cultural backpack&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}